ve coveted right  now so that is still a vast level of  viral transmission and presence in the  in in the country so we just don't know  yet what the remaining drift and  mutations could be  is the government ready to scale up in  the way it did before  should another virus come along  that really threatens  the the public well a lot of the scale  up has been done so part of what our job  was in 2020 was to put those  plans in place so we um  uh basically took the existing ecosystem  for vaccine manufacturing and scale up  um and nine different sites around the  country we have now  uh funded to scale up into much more  significant  capability so we've got a lot more  capability here now you talked about  having someone in government that's  responsible for this yes i mean i think  we should be treating it like we treat  defense because you know we're much more  likely to get a another serious pandemic  than we are to be invaded by somebody  yes but really serious not just a  cabinet minister yeah absolutely okay  and it needs to be somebody ideally um  uh that comes in i think that needs to  have that private sector experience have  you suggested that's the pm yeah yeah of  course and what did he say oh they you  know they'll take all those suggestions  well ultimately  transpires i don't know  do you think  that we have finally killed the  stereotype  that science is a boy's subject i mean  there's a lot of very very punchy women  who were absolutely instrumental in  in the whole initial covid response  no i don't and i think it's partly  because  we don't  uh teach our kids in school as to what  the what you can do in science so people  i still think think of scientists as  being you know men in white coats well  actually it's not that if you think  about what we're dealing with in  technology whether it's phone apps or  cyber security or how do you deal with  climate change and as soon as you start  saying well all of those are underpin  underpinned by scientific understanding  actually that's what's going to get  people excited because these new you  know younger people now they absolutely  want to help um save the world do you  think it's a coincidence that the people  heavily involved in  um  this vaccine were women  i think women are very good at problem  solving and just getting on with it as  you did well look thank you so much  thanks kate for talking to me i  appreciate it pleasure thanks for having  me  well that's all for today's show thank  you to all our guests fatali klitschko  christopher steele and dame kate bingham  and if you scan the qr code on your  screen right now you can listen to the  beth rigby interviews podcast a new  episode will be available later tonight  each week i take a look at the  highlights of the interviews and there's  some extra behind the bits scenes start  setting too  that's on the sky news app or wherever  you get your podcast
 

